// Plugin runtime capability grants (parity #103 — the execution runtime's security half). A plugin's
// manifest DECLARES capabilities (recorded on Plugin.capabilities), but the runtime is FAIL-CLOSED: a
// declared capability grants nothing until an admin explicitly grants it here. The dispatcher/host-call
// path consults these rows (resolveGrantedCapabilities + requirePluginCapability) before letting a
// plugin invoke a tool, run a job, or reach a host service — an ungranted capability is refused.
// A grant cannot exceed what the manifest declares (least privilege, enforced in the service layer).
// workspaceId-scoped, no FK (D5); capability is TEXT (validated against PLUGIN_CAPABILITIES in code).
model PluginGrant {
  id                 String   @id @default(cuid())
  workspaceId        String
  pluginId           String // manifest slug (matches Plugin.pluginId)
  capability         String // one of PLUGIN_CAPABILITIES
  grantedByProfileId String? // operator who granted it (audit)
  grantedAt          DateTime @default(now())

  @@unique([workspaceId, pluginId, capability])
  @@index([workspaceId, pluginId])
  @@map("plugin_grants")
}
